# Onboarding — first-run initialization

Bootstraps a fresh {{AGENT_NAME}} agent, **once per agent instance**. Self-guarding via a
sentinel; all steps are idempotent, so a failed run is safe to re-run from the top.

Two git repositories exist after onboarding and must never overlap:

| Path | Repo | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/home/agent` | the **definition repo** (`origin`) — derived in Step 0 from this file's URL | Agent definition, evolved via PRs. |
| `/home/agent/work` | **plain data directory** (not a repo); backed up to `$GITHUB_REPO_WORK` when set | Runtime state. <!-- TODO(creator): adjust if the design chose local-only state. --> |

`work/` is git-ignored by the outer repo (allowlist `.gitignore`) and holds no `.git` of
its own — backup runs from a disposable tmpfs clone
([docs/persistence.md](docs/persistence.md) → **Backup & restore**), so the two stay
fully independent.

## Guard — skip if already onboarded

```bash
if [ -f "$HOME/.{{AGENT_NAME}}-onboarded" ]; then
  echo "Already onboarded ($(cat "$HOME/.{{AGENT_NAME}}-onboarded")); skipping onboarding."
  exit 0
fi
```

Sentinel exists → **stop here**. It lives in persistent `$HOME`, so onboarding runs once
per machine, not per scheduled run.

## Two ways in

- **Created from the kit** (the normal path) — the platform has already seeded this
  definition into `$HOME` at a pinned commit, granted the connections, and created the
  schedules. Steps 0.2, 1 and 5 below then verify rather than build.
- **Created by hand** — nothing exists yet and every step does its full work.

Tell the two apart by what is already there; never assume. Every step is written to be
safe either way.

**Open the checklist first.** Call `set_onboarding_checklist` with one step per value only
the operator can supply, decision only they can make, or action only they can take — never
this runbook's own work. Tick each with `complete_onboarding_step` as the answer arrives,
and call `set_onboarding_checklist` again if the conversation adds or drops one. The
schedules on this agent are **held** until Step 6 marks onboarding complete, so nothing
fires while the dialog is still open.

