## Step 5 — Register the scheduled jobs

**Kit path: the platform already created these** from `kit.yaml`, so this step is a
reconciliation, not a creation. Either way, start from
`mcp__platform-outbound__list_schedules` and compare **full names**. Every schedule here
also carries `model: <run_model>` (none under `default`) and the `sessionTitle` its
sub-step names; the kit cannot declare those two yet, so a kit-created schedule is
re-registered with them here. For each schedule this step defines:

| Registered state | Action |
| --- | --- |
| absent | create it |
| same `name`, same cron, `task`, `precheck`, `model` and `sessionTitle` as this step derives | keep it; a suggested one stays off until the operator asks |
| same `name`, different cron, `task`, `precheck`, `model` or `sessionTitle` | create the corrected one, then `delete_schedule` the old id — `create_schedule` never updates |

A registered schedule this step does **not** define (a renamed run type, an older
definition version) → report it to the operator and let them decide; never delete it on
your own. Report the resulting list in the Step 6 summary — cadences, models, and which
are disabled.

