Never use an in-process cron — only platform schedules survive restarts and are visible to
the operator.

Create each missing schedule with `name: {{AGENT_NAME}}-<runtype>-<cadence-shorthand>`,
`sessionMode: fresh`, the same `precheck` its `kit.yaml` entry declares, `model` and
`sessionTitle` as above, and this task text pattern:

> <Run name>. The precheck already ran the pre-flight and found work: read the worklist
> JSON at the path its output names, and never run preflight.sh again this run. If the
> prompt carries no worklist path, run `bash "$HOME/scripts/preflight.sh" <mode>`
> yourself. Then follow CLAUDE.md → "<run section>": read exactly the worklist's
> read_set, <the run's action summary>, and back up work/ at the end with
> `bash "$HOME/scripts/work-backup.sh" persist` when $GITHUB_REPO_WORK is set.

## Step 6 — Record the version, write the sentinel, verify, release, report

Only after all previous steps succeeded. `work/VERSION` records the adopted definition
version (used by the version check — docs/persistence.md → **Definition version &
upgrade**):

```bash
head -1 "$HOME/VERSION" > "$HOME/work/VERSION"
date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ > "$HOME/.{{AGENT_NAME}}-onboarded"
```

The sentinel goes first so a failure in the verification below does not re-run the whole
runbook — the repair loop is the verification's own.

Then write the agent manifest: follow `docs/manifest.md` → **Write, check, publish**
(the card in `work/manifest.json`, published under `agent_manifest: dam`) and create
`work/PEERS.md` with the operator's rows from Step 3.

Then verify that onboarding produced the structure the templates promise — offline
first, then the live end-to-end pass:

```bash
bash "$HOME/scripts/verify-onboarding.sh" --live
```

Apply every `FAIL` line's `fix:` and re-run until it prints `PASS`; report any remaining
`warn` to the operator. Onboarding is not complete while it fails.

**Then release the schedules.** Tick the last checklist item and call
`mark_onboarding_complete` — only now, with the verification green and the configuration
genuinely in place. Until this call every schedule on the agent is held and records
`held: onboarding not complete`; after it they fire normally. It is idempotent, and the
platform verifies nothing about it — the stamp has the standing of the agent's own word,
so never make it to move a stuck run along.

Then give the operator a short **onboarding summary** in the chat UI:

1. The final `work/CONFIG.md` (verbatim).
2. What runs where: schedules and cadences, the model every scheduled session runs on,
   whether anonymous issues go to the definition repo, state persistence mode.
3. Day-to-day usage: <!-- TODO(creator): 3-5 bullets — how work gets triggered, how a
   human requests a re-run, how feedback is given, what can be changed later in chat
   (and which keys cannot). -->

From now on the guard short-circuits and normal runs follow `CLAUDE.md`.
